From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:55:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: the npln test writes its catalog where it can

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The test wrote its catalog to a relative "build/t_npln.tsv" and never checked fopen: the macOS CI runs the
 binary from the repository root, so that path did not exist, fopen returned NULL and the fprintf after it
 crashed the process with SIGSEGV (exit 139) before the test printed anything at all. The file now goes to
 TMPDIR (or /tmp) under a name of its own, and a failure to open it is reported instead of dereferenced.
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

---
 dm/host/tests/t_npln_patch.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/tests/t_npln_patch.c b/dm/host/tests/t_npln_patch.c
index 5b5b1f3..2166cd3 100644
--- a/dm/host/tests/t_npln_patch.c
+++ b/dm/host/tests/t_npln_patch.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #include "dm.h"
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <unistd.h>   // getpid
 
 module_t *g_mod;
 int g_nmod;
@@ -19,8 +20,13 @@ int main(void) {
     memset(g_image, 0, sizeof g_image);
     g_image[off] = 0xAA; g_image[off + 1] = 0xE2; g_image[off + 2] = 0x40; g_image[off + 3] = 0x39;
 
-    const char *path = "build/t_npln.tsv";
+    // A path of its own: the CI runs this binary from the repo root, so a relative "build/..." is not
+    // the folder the binary sits in - fopen came back NULL there and the fprintf below walked into it.
+    char path[512];
+    const char *tmp = getenv("TMPDIR");
+    snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s/t_npln_%d.tsv", tmp && *tmp ? tmp : "/tmp", (int)getpid());
     FILE *f = fopen(path, "w");
+    if (!f) return fail("cannot write the catalog");
     fprintf(f, "V\t0100965017338000\t2.3.0\tnpln\t1\n");
     fprintf(f, "P\t0100965017338000\t2.3.0\tD70CE1726C979E45ED4200E9C2B23B2A258FDC18000000000000000000000000"
                "\tmain\t128\tAAE24039\t2A008052\n");
